d sum over Y, its aligned four-sets are the aligned four-subsets of Y, and hence no real number is the second exchange moment of every balanced half.  The same identification gives the exchange spectrum at a half as the product of X - (1 - \u03b1\u1d62\u00b2/q) over the eigenvalues of the submatrix on that half, and at order six the characteristic polynomial (X - 1/5)(X - 4/5)\u00b2 for every three-element subset.",
